From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: the deferred split shrinker is no slab shrinker

With cgroup.memory=nokmem, on the headset's command line, only a shrinker flagged SHRINKER_NONSLAB
may be aware of memory cgroups. Without the flag the deferred split shrinker loses that awareness and
keeps the id 0, while its list stays per cgroup: a game's first huge page then warned in
set_shrinker_bit (id 0, a map of 0), and a cgroup's partly mapped huge pages were not split under
memory pressure.
---
--- a/mm/huge_memory.c
+++ b/mm/huge_memory.c
@@ -1024,7 +1024,8 @@
 static int __init thp_shrinker_init(void)
 {
 	deferred_split_shrinker = shrinker_alloc(SHRINKER_NUMA_AWARE |
-						 SHRINKER_MEMCG_AWARE,
+						 SHRINKER_MEMCG_AWARE |
+						 SHRINKER_NONSLAB,
 						 "thp-deferred_split");
 	if (!deferred_split_shrinker)
 		return -ENOMEM;
